1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,400
Every byte that leaves this stack is written down before it can leave.

2
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:12,217
The data-flow disclosure lists each flow: where it goes, what it carries, what it never carries, and how to switch it off.

3
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:17,253
And the build enforces it: a service without a row is refused.

4
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:21,197
When you talk to the twin, what leaves your device?

5
00:00:21,247 --> 00:00:26,658
Your typed words, the last few turns, and the address and browser every request carries.

6
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:33,009
Never audio, the avatar, a cookie, or any identifier of the visit or the visitor.

7
00:00:33,059 --> 00:00:37,191
And in production, no one's words land in any log, trace, or store.

8
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:42,695
When the paid fallback answers, your words go to Anthropic.

9
00:00:42,745 --> 00:00:50,516
In Hareet's words: this site saves none of it, and Anthropic may keep a turn it answered for up to thirty days, never for training.

10
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,736
Then, what the twin says back.

11
00:00:53,786 --> 00:00:57,980
It answers only from what Hareet wrote, and when that doesn't hold the answer, it says:

12
00:00:58,030 --> 00:00:59,623
"I don't know yet."

13
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:07,988
Before any word leaves the gateway, code checks the answer against its sources: numbers, amounts, ownership, privacy.

14
00:01:08,038 --> 00:01:10,055
A failed check withholds the answer.

15
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:20,388
And every change is tested: a hundred and eighty-six cases drawn from the corpus, graded by code, never by another model.

16
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:25,808
Every data flow disclosed. Built in the open, at hareet dot A I.
